  "title": "A knot builds exactly self-similar space in every dimension",
  "subject": "Which knots reproduce themselves exactly on every Sierpinski simplex of every dimension",
  "conclusion": "The standing wave (-1)^(x_0) sin(theta E)/sin(theta) reproduces itself exactly on every level-k Sierpinski d-simplex, with a factor that is a monic integer polynomial in 2 cos(theta), equal to 2^N at theta = 0 and never zero at odd prime-power angles. Its Legendre member is an exact knot in every dimension d >= 2, and in odd d the whole family is, so knots build exact self-similar spaces whose dimension rises to d in every dimension.",
